---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About — icanspeak.it" description="Why icanspeak.it exists: a small, independent site about etymology, made for people who like being surprised by their own language." altHref="/de/about/">
  <section class="about-hero">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">About this site</p>
      <h1>We think words deserve a second look</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Most of us use tens of thousands of words a week without ever asking where they came from. icanspeak.it
        is a small, ad-light project built for the moments you do ask — and for the rabbit holes that follow.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-body">
    <div class="container container--narrow prose">
      <h2>What we actually do here</h2>
      <p>
        We write short, sourced deep dives into individual words and language patterns: where a word was
        coined, how it drifted between languages, why two unrelated tongues sometimes converge on the same
        idea, and why "false friends" trip up even fluent speakers. Alongside the blog, the
        <a href="/words/">word cards</a> are a lighter format — a wall of bite-sized origin stories you can
        flip through in a few minutes.
      </p>

      <h2>Why etymology, specifically</h2>
      <p>
        Etymology is one of the few fields where history, migration, trade, colonization, and plain human
        gossip all leave physical fingerprints you can still read today, just by looking closely at a word.
        A single word like "ketchup" carries a trade route across three continents. A word like "nostalgia"
        carries a 17th-century medical diagnosis. Once you start noticing this, it's hard to stop.
      </p>

      <h2>What this site isn't</h2>
      <p>
        We're not a dictionary, a grammar course, or a language-learning app — there are better tools for
        that already. We're closer to a magazine: opinionated, occasionally speculative where the historical
        record is thin (we say so when it is), and written for curiosity rather than fluency.
      </p>

      <h2>A note on the domain</h2>
      <p>
        icanspeak.it started life as a language-training consultancy for professionals in Germany. That
        project's site is still online — we didn't want that work to disappear when the domain changed
        direction — and you can find it preserved at
        <a href="/former-site/">icanspeak.it/former-site</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about-hero { padding-block-start: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem); padding-block-end: 0; }
  .container--narrow { max-width: 42rem; }
  .about-hero h1 { margin-block: 0.75rem 1rem; }
  .about-body .prose h2 { margin-block: 2rem 0.75rem; }
  .about-body .prose p { margin-block-end: 1.25rem; max-width: 100%; }
  .about-body .prose a { color: var(--color-primary); text-decoration: underline; }
</style>
